It is morning in Copenhagen.
I am standing out in the hallway.
I am standing at a door.
It is my own door.
I have my own apartment now.
Nina lives on the same floor.
I stand with a key in my hand.
I put the key in the lock.
But it sticks.
I jiggle the key a little.
Then it turns.
The door opens.
I look inside.
"This is mine," I say.
I smile.
I step inside my new apartment.
